ek</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ryckman</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><name><surname>Ritchie</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Alternative cross-over strategies and selection techniques for grammatical evolution optimized neural networks</article-title><conf-name>GECCO &#x02018;06: Proceedings of the 8th annual conference on Genetic and evolutionary computation</conf-name><fpage>947</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><publisher-loc>New York, NY U.S.A</publisher-loc><publisher-name>ACM Press</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-cin-6-0433"><label>12</label><mixed-citation publication-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilbert</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Reif</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>A statistical comparison of grammatical evolution strategies in the domain of human genetics</article-title><conf-name>Proceedings of the 2005 IEEE Congress on Evolutionary Computation</conf-name><volume>1</volume><fpage>491</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Edinburgh</surname><given-names>UK</given-names></name></person-group><publisher-name>IEEE Press</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-cin-6-0433"><label>13</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>de Castro</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name><name><surname>Timmis</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><source>Artificial Immune Systems: A New Computational Intelligence Approach</source><publisher-name>Springer</publisher-name></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-cin-6-0433"><label>14</label><mixed-cit